              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","KL","H"] },
            { text: "therefore the rectangle {CD} by {AB} is commensurable with the square on {H}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","AB","H"] },
            { text: "But the square on {G} equals the rectangle {CD} by {AB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["G","CD","AB"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {G} is commensurable with the square on {H}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["G","H"] },
            { text: "But the square on {H} is rational, therefore the square on {G} is also rational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["H","G"] },
            { text: "Therefore {G} is rational. And it is the side of the rectangle {CD} by {AB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["G","CD","AB"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if an area is contained by an apotome and the binomial straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"] },
            { text: "the terms of which are commensurable with the terms of the apotome and in the same ratio,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CE","ED","AF","FB"] },
            { text: "then the side of the area is rational.",
              visible: ALL,
